              <td class="p-3">Built for it: no IT, Texas rules</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The honest read: enterprise platforms are the right call for multi-site health systems with IT and scheduling
        staff. Configure-it-yourself AI products fit hospitals with a dedicated scheduler who has time to run them.
        Neither describes a 25-bed critical access hospital, which is the gap an AI-native nurse scheduling service is
        built for. See the full buyer view in <a href="/critical-access-hospital-scheduling"
          >critical access hospital scheduling</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>How Does SimpleScheduleAI Deliver AI Nurse Scheduling as a Service?</h2>
